.TH LINDESKD 8 "2026" "lindesk 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lindeskd \- lindesk QoS broker (desktop responsiveness governor)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lindeskd
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-state\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-telemetry\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR FILTER ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-dbus ]
.br
.B lindeskd \-\-restore
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lindeskd
is the privileged half of lindesk, a userspace QoS governor that keeps the application
you are using responsive while builds, copies and indexers run in the background.
It runs as root under systemd
.RI ( lindeskd.service ,
.BR Type=notify ,
with a watchdog) and owns
.B org.lindesk.Broker1
on the system bus.
.PP
It probes the host's capabilities, watches PSI, hosts system plugins, runs the policy
pipeline (sensors, classifiers, policies, the resolver with safety caps, actuators,
sinks), applies settings to system units, enables iocost when
.B io.iocost = "auto"
and sends each user's desired settings to their
.BR lindesk\-session (1)
agent with the
.B UserState
signal.
.PP
Every change is runtime-only. The original values are recorded in
.I /run/lindesk/state.json
and restored on exit, after a crash
.RB ( ExecStopPost=lindeskd\ \-\-restore ),
or with
.BR "lindeskctl restore \-\-system" .
Interactive work is never made dangerous: no realtime classes, floors on every throttle,
and critical workloads can be boosted but never throttled.
.PP
At startup it checks its requirements (cgroup v2 or v1 controllers, PSI, privileges) and
exits with status 78 when one fails; see
.BR "lindeskctl doctor \-\-preflight" .
.B SIGHUP
reloads the configuration and plugins (as does the
.B Reload
D-Bus method);
.B SIGTERM
restores everything and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Configuration file (default
.IR /etc/lindesk/lindesk.toml ).
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " DIR"
Where the applied state and saved iocost settings live (default
.IR /run/lindesk ).
.TP
.BI \-\-telemetry\-dir " DIR"
Telemetry lake (default
.B telemetry.dir
or
.IR /var/lib/lindesk/telemetry ).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Observe only: compute, record and explain, but apply nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " FILTER"
Log filter (else
.BR RUST_LOG ,
else
.BR info ).
Logs go to the journal when started by systemd, else to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dbus
Don't own the bus name (testing).
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Revert every setting recorded in the state file (and the saved iocost settings), then exit.
Idempotent; exit status 1 when something could not be restored.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH D-BUS
.B org.lindesk.Broker1
at
.IR /org/lindesk/Broker1 :
.BR RegisterSession ,
.BR ReportForeground ,
.BR Interaction ,
.BR SetClass ,
.BR GetStatus ,
.BR Explain ,
.B Reload
and the
.B UserState
signal. Callers are identified by their bus credentials and authorized with polkit
.RB ( org.lindesk.set\-class\-own ,
.BR org.lindesk.set\-class\-any ,
.BR org.lindesk.manage ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/lindesk/lindesk.toml
Configuration. Every key has a default; check it with
.BR "lindeskctl config check \-\-system" .
.TP
.I /usr/share/lindesk/rules.d/ /etc/lindesk/rules.d/
Classifier rules.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/lindesk/plugins/ /etc/lindesk/plugins/
System plugins. Loaded only when root-owned and not group- or world-writable.
.TP
.I /run/lindesk/state.json
Applied settings with their original values.
.TP
.I /var/lib/lindesk/telemetry/
System telemetry lake (Parquet; readable by group
.BR lindesk ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lindeskctl (1),
.BR lindesk\-session (1),
.BR lindesk\-data (1),
.BR systemd.resource\-control (5)
